@startuml
title SIC/XE Event Architecture - Ownership and Reversible State

top to bottom direction

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 35

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor White
    BorderColor Black
    ArrowColor Black
}

hide empty members
set namespaceSeparator none


package "Host / Simulator" {

    class Simulator {
        - memory : Memory
        - registers : Registers
        - eventManager : EventManager
        + step()
        + undo()
        + redo()
    }

    class EventManager {
        - state : SimulatorEventState
        - history : IEvent[]
        - activeOrder : EventIndex[]
        - cursor : size_t
        + execute(event)
        + undo()
        + redo()
        + events_since(index)
        + cursor()
    }

    class SimulatorEventState {
        + memory : Memory
        + registers : Registers
    }
}


package "Architecture Plugin API" {

    interface InstructionExecutor {
        + execute(event)
    }

    interface IEvent {
        + mutates()
        + commit(state)
        + restore(state)
        + serialize()
    }

    class MemoryAccessor {
        + read(address, size)
        + write(address, bytes)
        + fetch(address, size)
    }

    class RegisterAccessor {
        + read(register)
        + write(register, value)
    }

    class SICXE {
        + step()
    }

    class DecodedInstruction {
        - address
        - bytes
        - format
        - flags
        - displacement
        - target
        - resolved_operand
        - executor
        + execute()
    }
}


package "Event Model" {

    abstract class StateMutation {
        + mutates() = true
        + commit(state)
        + restore(state)
    }

    abstract class Observation {
        + mutates() = false
        + commit(state)
        + restore(state)
    }

    package "State Mutations" {

        class MemoryWrite {
            - address
            - old_value
            - value
        }

        class RegisterWrite {
            - register
            - old_value
            - value
        }
    }

    package "Execution Observations" {

        class MemoryRead {
            - address
            - value
        }

        class RegisterRead {
            - register
            - value
        }

        class InstructionFetched {
            - address
            - bytes
        }

        class InstructionDecoded {
            - address
            - bytes
            - format
            - flags
            - displacement
            - target
            - resolved_operand
        }
    }
}


' Ownership

Simulator *-- Memory
Simulator *-- Registers
Simulator *-- EventManager

EventManager *-- SimulatorEventState
EventManager *-- "0..*" IEvent : owns

SimulatorEventState --> Memory
SimulatorEventState --> Registers


' Event hierarchy

IEvent <|.. StateMutation
IEvent <|.. Observation

StateMutation <|-- MemoryWrite
StateMutation <|-- RegisterWrite

Observation <|-- MemoryRead
Observation <|-- RegisterRead
Observation <|-- InstructionFetched
Observation <|-- InstructionDecoded


' Execution facade

EventManager ..|> InstructionExecutor

SICXE --> InstructionExecutor : submits events
DecodedInstruction --> InstructionExecutor : submits events

SICXE --> MemoryAccessor
SICXE --> RegisterAccessor
SICXE --> DecodedInstruction : creates

DecodedInstruction --> MemoryAccessor : operand access
DecodedInstruction --> RegisterAccessor : register access


' Accessors submit events

MemoryAccessor --> InstructionExecutor : MemoryRead / MemoryWrite / InstructionFetched
RegisterAccessor --> InstructionExecutor : RegisterRead / RegisterWrite


' Event application

EventManager ..> IEvent : execute / commit / restore

MemoryWrite ..> Memory : modifies
RegisterWrite ..> Registers : modifies

MemoryRead ..> Memory : observes
RegisterRead ..> Registers : observes


note right of EventManager
    Event execution:

    execute(event)
        |
        v
    event.commit(state)
        |
        v
    append to history
        |
        v
    advance cursor

    Undo:
    event.restore(state)

    Redo:
    event.commit(state)
end note


note right of StateMutation
    Reversible state change.

    Stores both:

    old_value
    new_value

    Undo applies old_value.
    Redo applies new_value.
end note


note right of Observation
    Non-mutating execution trace.

    Records what the CPU
    read, fetched, or decoded.

    Does not modify simulator state.
end note


note bottom of EventManager
    The event history is append-only.

    The cursor identifies the current
    position in the active execution path.

    Undo moves the cursor backward.
    Redo moves the cursor forward.

    A new execution after undo creates
    a new active execution path.
end note

@enduml